הַשּׁ ׳מֶּתַח Judg 9:40 + (see ׳פ ), הַשּׁ ׳דַּלְתוֺת 1Sam 21:14 + (see ׳ד 3 ); ׳מֶּתַחהַֿשּׁ Judg 18:16-17 , of farm or village; so of camp Exod 32:26-27 , (J). In cities, elaborate structure, with roof 2Sam 18:24 , upper chamber 19:1 ; compare רָאשֵׁיכֶם שְׁעָרִים שְׂאוּ Psa 24:7 ; 24:9 ; write laws ׳בִּשׁ Deut 6:9 ( + בֵּיתֶ֑ךָ עַלמְֿזֻזוֺת ), 11:20 (+ id. .); הַשּׁ ׳בְּתוֺךְ 1Sam 9:18 , הַשּׁ ׳אֶלאתּוֺךְ 2Sam 3:27 ; שׁ ׳(לְ)יַד as public, 1Sam 4:18 , + 4:13 ᵐ5 Th We Dr and others, compare 2Sam 15:2 ; 18:4 ; Prov 8:3 (|| פְתָחִים מְבוֺא ). b. particular gates of Jerusalem are: -1 ׳שׁ אֶפְרַיִם 3b ); (16) ׳שׁ הַמִּנָּה 2Kin 14:13 || 2Chr 25:23 (read הַמִּנָּה for הַמּוֺנֶה ), Jer 31:38 ; 2Chr 26:9 ; probably = ׳שׁ הַמִּנִּים Zech 14:10 ; -17 ׳שׁ הַצּאֹן Neh 3:1 , 32 ; 12:39 ; -18 ׳שׁ הָרִאשׁוֺן Zech 14:10 ; &#8212; on sites and related to each other see RS-GASm Ency. Bib. JERUSALEM Conder Hast. DB id. Buhl G 133 ff. Bd Pal. under the word Murray Hd. Bk, under the word BeRy Ne p. 182 ff. Gu ZPV , especially v (1882). 7 ff. viii (1885), 245 ff. Comm. on the passage variant reading c. of Ezekiel's holy city , הָעִיר שַׁעֲרֵי Ezek 48:31 , three on each side, named for tribes, 48:31 ; 48:31 ; 48:31 ; 48:31 12 t. Ezekiel 48.. 2. a. gate = space inside gate, as public meeting-place, market 2Kin 7:1 , 18 , place of public well 2Sam 23:15-16 , = 1Chr 11:17-18 , where elders, judges, king, sat officially Deut 21:19 ; 22:15 ; Amos 5:12 , 15 ; Isa 29:21 ; 2Sam 18:24 ; 19:9 ; 1Kin 22:10 2Chr 18:9 ; Gen 19:1 (J) Prov 24:7 ; Job 5:4 ; 31:21 ; Ruth 4:1 (twice in verse); Prov 31:23 , 31 , etc.; of conqueror Jer 1:15 ; apparently = שׁ ׳רְחוֺב Gen 19:2 (J) Neh 8:16 ; 1Chr 9:16 + (see I. ׳ר ); Gen 34:20 (P) one came unto gate ( אֶלֿ בָּא ), so שׁ ׳בָּאֵי 23:10 , 18 (P) those entering the gate , i.e. having citizens' rights; also went out (to), שׁ ׳יָצָא Job 29:7 (i.e., in this case, from his own house, outside the city), hence שׁ ׳כָּליֹֿצְאֵי Gen 34:24 (twice in verse) (P; compare also אֶלֿ הוֺצִיא Deut 21:19 ; 22:15 , 24 ); hence = body of citizens, עַמִּי׳כָּלשֿׁ Ruth 3:11 . b. hence also = city Isa 14:31 (|| עִיר ), Psa 87:2 , etc. c. specifically in Deuteronomy, בִּשְׁעָרֶיךָ in thy gates , i.e. thy cities, towns, etc., Deut 5:14 = Exod 20:10 ; Deut 12:12 , 15 , 17 , 21 22 t. Deuteronomy + 1Kin 8:37 (read שׁ ׳בְּאַחַד , compare Deut 18:6 ; 23:17 , so ᵑ6 ᵐ5 modern), so || 2Chr 6:28 , + (perhaps) Jer 14:2 (but 15:7 ; Nahum 3:13 figurative of gates as entrance to land); of private house, צַדִּיק שַׁעֲרֵי Prov 14:19 (perhaps compare Judg 18:16 1a above). 3. a. gate of royal castle or palace 2Kin 9:31 ; Jer 22:2 , 4 ; Neh 2:8 ; Est 2:19 10 t. Esther; specifically (of king of Judah), ׳שׁ סוּר 2Kin 11:6 = ׳שׁ הַיְסוֺד 2Chr 23:5 (see ׳יס ׳ס, ), ׳שׁ הָרָצִים 2Kin 11:19 , ׳הַשּׁ הָר ׳אַחַר 11:6 ; ׳שׁ הַמּ בֵּית ׳הַסּוּסִים 2Chr 23:15 ( = הַסּ ׳מְבוֺא || 2Kin 11:16 ); apparently of official residence, שׁ ׳מֶּתַח יְהוֺשֻׁעַ 23:8 . b. of temple Jer 7:2 (twice in verse); 1Chr 9:23 ; 16:42 12 t. Chronicles, including י מַחֲנוֺת ׳שַׁעֲרֵי 2Chr 31:2 (see מַחֲנֶה 1 , p. 334), compare Psa 100:4 ; 118:20 , צֶדֶק שַׁעֲרֵי Psalm 100:19; specifically ׳שׁ הָעֶלְיוֺן בִּנְיָמִין Jer 20:2 , and (omit ׳בִּנְי ) 2Kin 15:35 2Chr 27:3 ; Ezek 9:2 ; 2Chr 23:20 , ׳שׁ י ׳(בֵּית) הֶחָדָשׁ Jer 26:10 ; 36:10 , צָפוֺנָה ׳שׁ הַמּוֺנֶה הַמְּנִימִית Ezek 8:3 compare 8:14 , 8:5 , ׳שׁ י בֵּית שַׁעַר ׳הַמִּזְבֵּחַ הַקַּדְמֹנִי 10:19 ; 11:1 ; ׳שׁ שַׁלֶּכֶת 1Chr 26:16 ; הַמֶּלֶח שַׁעַר 9:18 . c. of Ezekiel's temple and courts Ezek 40:3 , 6 ; 44:11 , 17 67t. Ezekiel 40-47. d. of court of tabernacle (P), ׳שׁ הֶחָצֵר Exod 27:16 ; 35:17 + 6t. Exodus + Num 4:36 . 4 figurative שׁ ׳זֶה הַשָּׁמַיִם Gen 28:17 (E; || אֱלֹהִים בֵּית ); plural שְׁאוֺל שַׁעֲרֵי Isa 38:10 ; מָֿוֶת׳שׁ Job 38:17 ; Psa 9:14 ; 107:18 ; ׳שׁ צַלְמָוֶת Job 38:17 . תְּרַע noun [masculine] gate, door ( ᵑ7 Syriac; Biblical Hebrew שַׁ֫עַר , √I. שׁער ); — construct ׳ת : 1 door of furnace Dan 3:26 . 2 gate of king, i.e. palace, court, Dan 2:29 (compare Est 2:19 , see שַׁ֫